items.description:
`summary` carries `text`; every other kind carries `items` (at most 200):
`experience` — { title, employer, location?, start?, end?, current?, summary?, highlights? };
`education` — { school, credential?, field?, start?, end?, current?, summary? };
`projects` — { name, role?, url?, summary?, highlights?, skills? };
`skills` — { name?, keywords };
`other` — { heading?, lines? }, for certifications, awards, languages and the like.
Sections in `other` never count toward years of experience.

UnauthorizedError.description:
Unauthorized. This route accepts an API key or a session. It answers `401` when:

- the request carries no API key and comes from no whitelisted first-party `Origin` or
  `Referer` (`details.code` `API_KEY_REQUIRED`);
- a session cookie arrives with no `Origin` or `Referer` and is not a valid session
  (`details.code` `AUTH_REQUIRED`);
- the API key is malformed, unknown, revoked or expired (no `details`);
- a first-party request has no signed-in session (no `details`).
